> base(x: real, y: real) = (x + y) ^ 2
> basec(x: real, y: real) = x ^ 2 + 2 * x * y + y ^ 2
> equiv base basec
base and basec are equal on the domain of base (sampled, not proved; no SAT proof: a real value)
> swapped(x: real, y: real) = (y + x) ^ 2
> swappedc(x: real, y: real) = y * y + 2 * y * x + x * x
> equiv swapped swappedc
swapped and swappedc are equal on the domain of swapped (sampled, not proved; no SAT proof: a real value)
> expand (y + x) ^ 2 - (y * y + 2 * y * x + x * x)
  ucas: expand (y + x) ^ 2 - (y * y + 2 * y * x + x * x)
expand (y + x)^2 - (y*y + 2y*x + x*x)
  = 0
  check: exact (both sides have the same normal form)
